\name{CoverOrder}
\alias{CoverOrder}
\title{An entry with a compulsory stop and no target}
\description{
It behaves like a bracket without a target, except that the stop is required and a target is refused: the stop is armed on the first partial fill, grows as the entry fills, and is cancelled if the entry is cancelled with nothing filled. Brokers once sold this as a product, and Flattrade's API restricts it, which is why UBI rebuilds it. By default UBI holds a limit entry in its virtual order book until the other side of the book reaches its price, answering HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed}, while the exits rest at the broker as the entry fills; give \code{hold_limits} \code{FALSE} to send the entry at once. A stop the broker refuses cancels the rest of the entry, and the parent ends \code{failed}, because the position is left without its stop.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
